<p style="text-align: center;"><img src="/images/2012/Flash-layout.jpg" alt="Layout for a conformation portrait of a horse" width="600" height="479" /></p>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p>The start of a new painting. &nbsp;24x30 in oil on Claessens #12DP. &nbsp;I've outlined the horse in Conte crayon so that I can play around with the design and get the drawing down very accurately before putting paint on the canvas. &nbsp;I've erased most of the lines I used to place the critical anatomical points by wiping them off with OMS and a paper towel.</p>
<p>Later this week I will work over the outline in thin paint with a bit of Liquin in it, then work with a full color block-in.</p>